        <mxCell id="dlB1TXSmg05-ScG6FHXB-11" parent="1" style="shape=process;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;strokeColor=#0F8B8D;fontColor=#143642;fillColor=#FAE5C7;size=0.02127659574468085;rounded=0;" value="&lt;p&gt; in the following cobol copybooks the type is a 4 digit field called :SAWX-:SATZART. In the file AvO-Echt.txt the field starts at position 29:&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(20, 54, 66), rgb(173, 202, 213));&quot;&gt;S37F010K - F010,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(20, 54, 66), rgb(173, 202, 213));&quot;&gt;S37F020K - F020,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(20, 54, 66), rgb(173, 202, 213));&quot;&gt;S37F030K - F030&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(20, 54, 66), rgb(173, 202, 213));&quot;&gt;and so on.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Can you help interpret the data in the file based on the layout. please add copies not mentioned as required based on the naming as shown.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;" vertex="1">
